1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,260
Nails through his hands.

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:04,701
Soldiers at his feet, gambling for his clothes.

3
00:00:06,061 --> 00:00:08,681
And from the cross comes a word no one expected

4
00:00:08,701 --> 00:00:10,162
— not a curse.

5
00:00:10,402 --> 00:00:11,082
It is a prayer.

6
00:00:12,462 --> 00:00:15,062
As they divide his clothing, Jesus prays for

7
00:00:15,082 --> 00:00:16,843
the very people putting him to death.

8
00:00:17,423 --> 00:00:21,223
Father, forgive them; for they know not what

9
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:21,723
they do.

10
00:00:22,143 --> 00:00:24,924
Luke records it as they gambled: And they parted

11
00:00:24,964 --> 00:00:26,664
his raiment, and cast lots.

12
00:00:26,824 --> 00:00:29,364
"They know not what they do" does not excuse

13
00:00:29,424 --> 00:00:32,305
the sin; it intercedes for the sinner.

14
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:34,885
And the sin that put him there was ours too.

15
00:00:35,945 --> 00:00:38,726
He gave himself willingly — and the Lord who

16
00:00:38,766 --> 00:00:41,126
prayed for his executioners still lives to

17
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:42,706
make intercession for sinners.

18
00:00:42,906 --> 00:00:46,227
This is the gospel: while we were yet sinners,

19
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:49,547
Christ died for us — pleading mercy before

20
00:00:49,587 --> 00:00:50,568
we knew we needed it.

21
00:00:51,848 --> 00:00:55,508
That mercy is held out to you now: come, and

22
00:00:55,548 --> 00:00:56,929
receive it by faith.
